# As random-modes-1.test, with another seed. It has a partial term
# unified with a ground one by an implied mode, where mmc reports a mode
# error in its own unification procedure (GitHub issue 74), which the
# comparison ignores.
#
# REQUIRES: mmc
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir %t
# RUN: %python %S/../../../utils/type-oracle/generate-mode-programs.py --seed 12 --count 40 %t
# RUN: %compare-types --modes --error-lines %t/*.m
